~ start
# talk_to entry point for world-Layla (layla_advanced_overlay launches here).
# the chapter 2 intro cutscene does NOT come through here — chapter2_intro.dialogue
# imports this file and jumps straight to post_wake_intro with actors already staged.
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen") == true:
	=> companion_hub

# safety net: talked to before the intro somehow ran. stage the pair the way the
# cutscene hand-off would have, then play the intro.
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
=> post_wake_intro

~ post_wake_intro
# [post opening cutscene convo with us]
# reached from chapter2_intro.dialogue with Fiona (left) and Layla (right, flipped)
# already on stage over the dimmed live level.
Layla: Fionaaaa! You fell asleep while working again!
do actor_change("Layla", "angry_1")
Layla: How many times do I need to tell you that you need to rest properly!
Layla: In your own bed! In your own home!
do actor_change("Layla", "base")
Player: I know, I know.
Player: I just really got into it. Going home would've broken that flow.
Player: Also, what's this thing over me?
Layla: It's my jacket. I kept it over you to keep you warm as you slept.
Player: Oh.
Layla: Wait, lemme take it off you. I'll put it in my car later.
Player: Thanks, Layla.
Player: What time is it? Has the professor come in yet?
Layla: It's 7:30 right now. The professor doesn't come in until 10, usually.
do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
Layla: And um... Fiona. Would you still help me with what I asked you yesterday?
Layla: You know, the genomic sequencing thing?
Layla: The professor asked me to show him the results first thing after he arrived.
Layla: If I don't do that, I'm doomed!
do actor_change("Layla", "base")
Player: Sure. I can do that. Shouldn't take me more than ten minutes.
Player: You know that you could easily do it yourself though, right?
Player: Objectively, you're smarter than the average undergrad Research Assistant.
Player: If I can do it in 10 minutes, you should know it's possible for you to do in under an hour.
# layla is shy. TODO: swap for a proper shy expression when the art lands.
do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
Layla: Umm... I'm glad you think that.
# layla is extra shy
Layla: I would still like to have you do it for me once, if you don't mind...
Layla: I learn faster when you teach me.
Player: No worries. Let's get to the lab ASAP. I need to go home and shower after this.
do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
Layla: Yaaaaay! Thanks Fiona! I owe you one.
do actor_change("Layla", "base")
Player: Let's go.
do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen", true)
=> END

~ companion_hub
# in-world talk_to hub over the dimmed live level. both sprites are staged, mirroring
# the real-world arrangement: layla_character.gd sets layla_player_on_left when the
# interaction fires. facing convention matches the intro: left = unflipped, right = flipped.
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_player_on_left") == true:
	do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
	do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
	do actor_flip("Layla", true)
else:
	do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "left")
	do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "right")
	do actor_flip("Fiona", true)
Layla is following you with glistening eyes.
Her scent reminds you of lavenders drenched in dew.
You sense that she cares about you.
~ hub_return
do actor_change("Layla", "base")
What do you want to say to her?

- Ask her about work
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_asked_about_work", true)
	Player: You know, I'm happy to help you with this, but I have to ask...
	Player: Why didn't you do it sooner?
	Player: It makes sense to finish off difficult tasks way before deadlines.
	Player: As your mentor, I need to point this out.
	Player: We need to move fast if we want to secure funding.
	You notice her shoulders slump after hearing that remark.
	do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
	Layla: I know... I'm sorry.
	Layla: It's just... I was afraid of messing it up.
	Layla: The equipment is limited, and expensive.
	Layla: If I got it wrong, it would've come out of the lab's pocket.
	Layla: I didn't wanna disappoint the professor.
	Layla: Or... you.
	She looks away, but her mind's eye looks toward you.
	What do you wanna say to her?

	- Comfort her
		do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_work_comforted", true)
		Player: That's... alright.
		Player: I would only say that you need to believe in yourself more.
		Player: You're better at this than you realize.
		# TODO: shy expression when the art lands.
		do actor_focus("Layla", 1.6, 0.3)
		Layla: ....!
		Her face turns a bright red.
		Layla: Thank you, Fiona.
		Layla: I guess I needed to hear that.
		do actor_unfocus_all(0.4)
		Layla will remember this.
		do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
		Layla: Still, I promise I'll be more punctual!
		Layla: Can't disappoint my prodigal mentor, after all!
		Player: Yeah, yeah.
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

	- Reprimand her
		do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_work_reprimanded", true)
		Player: I get that, but you still should be more responsible.
		Player: The lab can cushion buying new equipment ruined by a junior assistant.
		Player: It won't be able to do that if we don't secure the next round of funding, though.
		Player: And that will happen. If we continue to move slow.
		do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
		Layla looks really dejected after hearing you say that.
		Layla: I'm sorry.
		Layla: I promise I'll be better.
		Player: Right.
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

- Ask her about her life
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_asked_about_life", true)
	Player: So... apart from work, what've you been up to lately?
	Layla: Whaaaaaa?
	Layla: You're asking me about something other than work!?
	Layla: Are you okay? Do you have a high temperature?
	Layla: Come here, lemme touch your forehead.
	Player: I'm okay, actually.
	Player: Guess I just... realized I hadn't asked you that in a minute.
	Layla will remember that.
	Layla: Oh... okay.
	Layla: Lemme see. Well...
	do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
	Layla: Oh, I watched this movie recently! Devil Wears Grada 2.
	Layla: Its prequel was my favorite movie of ALL TIME!!!
	do actor_change("Layla", "base")
	Player: Oh. I see. How'd you like this one then?
	Layla: It was....
	Layla: Okay? I guess.
	Layla: I mean, it had its moments, but it lacked something its genius prequel had, you know?
	Layla: I also feel it had too many product placements?
	do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
	Layla: Got a bit tiring seeing a cola can company be advertised for the third time...
	do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
	Layla: But ohmygod. The fashion in it!
	Layla: That remained top notch.
	do actor_change("Layla", "base")
	Layla: Okay, maybe it was just a lil' bit worse than the last one, if I'm being honest.
	Layla: But that was already such a high bar!
	All of a sudden, she seems more animated.
	Player: I didn't realize you liked fashion that much.
	Layla: That's because you never asked!
	Layla: ... Or maybe I didn't let it show.
	Layla: I dress pretty basic for someone who's into fashion this much.

	- Ask her why she does that
		do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
		Layla: Well, my parents are immigrants...
		Layla: Let's say they raised me in their own way.
		Layla: I was taught not to attract too much attention to myself.
		Layla: Whenever I've tried dressing up, it's led to a lot of mixed feelings, you know?
		Player: I see.
		Player: I'm sorry about that. I hope you can find your confidence someday.
		Player: For me, clothes are just a matter of convenience.
		Player: If I could, I'd roam around naked everywhere.
		Player: Unfortunately, that would land me in jail.
		# layla face zoomin - shy. TODO: shy expression when the art lands.
		do actor_focus("Layla", 1.6, 0.3)
		Layla: ...
		Player: Layla, you alright?
		Layla: No!
		Layla: I mean - Yes! No no.
		Player: Huh?
		Layla: Oh well, I think it's getting quite hot in here, hehe? What do you think about the weather? And what are your thoughts about the economic and political state of the world?
		do actor_unfocus_all(0.4)
		Player: Riiiight.
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

	- Move on
		Player: I see.
		Player: That's... interesting.
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

- Never mind [Leave]
	=> END
